{"file_path":"/home/john/mynotes/deterministic_equidistribution_theory/finite_spectral_shadows.tex","new_string":"The defect cocycle relocates rather than removes the difficulty, but the\nfinite-operator side is now substantially a theorem. The rigorous core comprises\nthe sliding-window congruence; the proof that the quadratic character is\nvaluation parity in disguise, hence an exact coboundary; the \\emph{classification}\n$\\operatorname{Cob}=\\langle\\chi_2\\rangle$ (\\cref{thm:class}), which makes the\nnon-coboundary quotient canonical rather than conjectural; the strict spectral\ngap at every finite level (\\cref{cor:strict}); the conductor collapse\n(\\cref{thm:collapse}), which reduces uniformity in $Q$ to the single computable\nsequence $\\gamma_c(s)$; and the height-strip rotation identity\n(\\cref{prop:rot}). The remaining finite-operator task is exactly one statement,\n\\cref{conj:ext} (bounded-conductor extremality, $\\sup_c\\gamma_c<1$), with\nprincipal-unit cancellation as the natural route. The genuinely quenched\narrow---bad orbit $\\Rightarrow$ finite non-coboundary spectral shadow---remains\nthe open keystone.","old_string":"The defect cocycle relocates rather than removes the difficulty. The\nreorganisations of known structure are in hand---the sliding-window congruence,\nthe annealed Fourier gap, and (the new rigorous core) the proof that the\nquadratic character is valuation parity in disguise, hence an exact coboundary.\nThis forces the correct statement of the finite spectral hypothesis: a gap for\nall \\emph{non-coboundary} characters of the faithful synchronized operator,\nrelative to the valuation-pushforward residue reference. On that quotient the gap\nis observed to be constant and conductor-controlled, and the remaining\nfinite-operator task is the precise pair \\cref{conj:nocob,conj:mono} (no further\ncoboundaries; conductor monotonicity / principal-unit cancellation). The genuinely\nquenched arrow---bad orbit $\\Rightarrow$ finite non-coboundary spectral shadow---\nremains the open keystone.","replace_all":false}